From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdiplus: bicubic and high quality interpolation; bold and italic font metrics

Images drawn with InterpolationModeBicubic, HighQuality, HighQualityBilinear
or HighQualityBicubic were sampled bilinearly ("Unimplemented
interpolation"), so pictures and thumbnails drawn smaller by .NET
WinForms, Paint-style programs and photo viewers aliased into moire and
jagged edges where Windows draws them smooth. The family metrics ignored
the font style ("ignoring style").

- Bicubic: a 4x4 cubic convolution (Keys, a = -0.5) on premultiplied
  colour, kept within what the alpha allows.
- HighQuality, HighQualityBicubic, HighQualityBilinear: drawn smaller,
  each destination pixel averages its footprint in the source (a
  prefilter, up to 16x16 samples along the transformed axes); drawn
  larger, a bicubic (or bilinear) sample. The sampled area takes the
  kernel's reach; samples past it come from its edge.
- Default and LowQuality stay bilinear, as on Windows.
- GdipGetLineSpacing, GdipGetCellAscent, GdipGetCellDescent and
  GdipGetEmHeight read the bold, italic or bold italic face's metrics
  (hhea, or OS/2) when the family has that face, cached per family.

Wine's gdiplus tests: font 868, graphics 5610, image 4923, metafile 1929
tests, no failures, as before.

Gate: test/gdipquality-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/gdipquality-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_PREFILTER, SG_MUTANT_BICUBIC_AS_BILINEAR
(gdiplus/graphics.c), SG_MUTANT_STYLE_IGNORED (gdiplus/font.c).
---
--- a/dlls/gdiplus/font.c
+++ b/dlls/gdiplus/font.c
